  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Three teams – pass out and in",
  "description": "Mark out a square of about 15 × 15 metres. Three teams of three or four. One team stands on the sides of the square and may move along the line, one team is inside the square, and the third team, red, is also inside and chases the ball.\n\nThe two teams with the ball play together, but the passes must go out and in: a player on the side always passes to a player inside the square and the other way round. Two side players may not pass to each other. Count the passes out loud. When red win the ball, or it goes out of the square, the team that made the bad pass become the new chasers and red take their place. Beat the record for the session!\n\nVariants: decide which foot to use, at most two touches, or everyone must take two touches. Easier: allow passes between the side players. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Inside the square: keep moving so there is always a free passing lane to you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up before the ball arrives so you know where the next pass is going."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass to the foot furthest from the chaser."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Chasers: work together and close the passing lanes instead of everyone running at the ball."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
